er/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $C^T,$ if \n$[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/example-4386.json" "file_sha256" "08995625a93b2d43b33256d2e68fc5b2dbd3731febf8e9bf552ac60837317f9f" "basis" 1453 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the transpose, we interchange the rows and columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/example-4386.json" "file_sha256" "08995625a93b2d43b33256d2e68fc5b2dbd3731febf8e9bf552ac60837317f9f" "basis" 1453 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n    ${A} = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        5 & -1 & 0 \\\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack,$\nthen what is ${A^T} ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/example-4387.json" "file_sha256" "3466e1b17c648cabcf1fa818baa7a19eaf8871a1b656f7ba8b79510b395f4a5d" "basis" 1453 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the transpose, we interchange the rows and columns. \n\nHere, there is just a single row, so it becomes a single column:\n\n$$\n{A}^T = \n    \t\t\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\t\\matrix {\n    5 \\ \n    -1 \\ \n    0 \\  \n    \t\t}\n    \t\t\\right\\rbrack\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/example-4387.json" "file_sha256" "3466e1b17c648cabcf1fa818baa7a19eaf8871a1b656f7ba8b79510b395f4a5d" "basis" 1453 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix\n    ${B} = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        1 & 2 & 4 & 2\\\n        4 & 4 & 1 & 1\\\n        3 & -3 & 0 & -1\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack.$\nWhat are the dimensions of ${B}^T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/example-4388.json" "file_sha256" "e2d450311d1947d10c3cd5b8242bcd50867a80e17102e546db7ea1c20ef435bf" "basis" 1453 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When a matrix is transposed, its dimensions switch from $N \\times M$ to $M \\times N.$\n\nSo, since $B$ is a $3 \\times 4$ matrix, the transpose ${B}^T$ is a $4\\times3$ matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/example-4388.json" "file_sha256" "e2d450311d1947d10c3cd5b8242bcd50867a80e17102e546db7ea1c20ef435bf" "basis" 1453 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-126129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value