"ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073808/state.json" "file_sha256" "f8c9c557ec2ca797701b8f65050959f0a9c8495167bda2f31232e5d46425e16a"} {"question" "e-4386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $C^T,$ if \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073808/assets/d5e344ac147321b0440d313274626b1a00527214467cbc85bac199c10fee00bd.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073808/example-4386.json" "file_sha256" "e385e57a8608a466b893aa8aeaa59fd85bfc81b4087f0bd21779666b645cc3d0"} {"question" "e-4386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the transpose, we interchange the rows and columns:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073808/assets/d64f16633ed91692b0cd22daa4c739a6e4347ec6c0596c992d28088880ea2862.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073808/example-4386.json" "file_sha256" "e385e57a8608a466b893aa8aeaa59fd85bfc81b4087f0bd21779666b645cc3d0"} {"question" "e-4387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n    ${A} = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        5 & -1 & 0 \\\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack,$\nthen what is ${A^T} ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073808/example-4387.json" "file_sha256" "c570732b6bcd934796c7b83f18f51a65bec286683c99907bb5ffab539ca1cbc2"} {"question" "e-4387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the transpose, we interchange the rows and columns. \n\nHere, there is just a single row, so it becomes a single column:\n\n$$\n{A}^T = \n    \t\t\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\t\\matrix {\n    5 \\ \n    -1 \\ \n    0 \\  \n    \t\t}\n    \t\t\\right\\rbrack\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073808/example-4387.json" "file_sha256" "c570732b6bcd934796c7b83f18f51a65bec286683c99907bb5ffab539ca1cbc2"} {"question" "e-4388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix\n    ${B} = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        1 & 2 & 4 & 2\\\n        4 & 4 & 1 & 1\\\n        3 & -3 & 0 & -1\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack.$\nWhat are the dimensions of ${B}^T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073808/example-4388.json" "file_sha256" "1fd64dd5bb7c1482ddb24377fde5525c30c8c04e6169528e5c6da69adfaee706"} {"question" "e-4388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When a matrix is transposed, its dimensions switch from $N \\times M$ to $M \\times N.$\n\nSo, since $B$ is a $3 \\times 4$ matrix, the transpose ${B}^T$ is a $4\\times3$ matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073808/example-4388.json" "file_sha256" "1fd64dd5bb7c1482ddb24377fde5525c30c8c04e6169528e5c6da69adfaee706"}] "usage" {"q-70065" [] "e-4387" [] "e-4386" [] "q-70068" [] "q-275365" [] "q-126130" [] "q-126136" [] "e-4388" []} "basis" 2747 "retractions" [[17592186059476 :question/problem "Find $C^T,$ if \n$[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]$"] [17592186059476 :question/worked-solution "To find the transpose, we interchange the rows and columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186308654 17592186308655 17592186308656 17592186308657 17592186308658 17592186308661 17592186308662 17592186308663 17592186308664 17592186308665 17592186308675 17592186308676 17592186308678 17592186308680 17592186308682 17592186308736 17592186308737 17592186308738 17592186308739 17592186308740 17592186308743 17592186308744 17592186308745 17592186308746 17592186308